/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/w10-knock/luna/out.md:16:**LEAD.** A per-face secret could key sovereign prefilter without adding credentials, if causal removal/roll rotates it. It cannot cover first dial. Route that first dial through the floor gate: it only needs public join-carriage/announcement behavior; no pre-seating request should reach sovereign authority. After join, its certified key can support a sovereign knock. Replay/freshness remains causal inside the encrypted exchange, never wall-clock based. A new HMAC relation should encode authentication only. Today the knock also selects dispatch; if that selection stays public and the prefilter becomes secret, split the relations/names. Alternatively keep public route selection and accept only its floor-tier leak.
