/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/w10-knock/luna/out.md:22:**LEAD.** A pin-keyed knock does not protect against a terminator log reader or gossiping Herm who also holds the pins: the observed candidate tag maps directly to the corresponding Nexus/route. That violates the named “nothing of one tier, Nexus or route links to another” aim (`:116`) if sovereign routes count. Teshima: Leilani joins Kalani's private council with two of three faces; the kept-back face must learn neither membership nor dial presence. A pin-holding terminator can correlate council membership from the sovereign path. Face-scoped knocks avoid sibling correlation, but pin holders still test their face. Gaia: at a family hearth, the public shelf remains intentionally discoverable; private council access should not advertise which Nexus path a member reached. Elyncia: a civic crossroads Herm should carry sealed bytes between shrines without learning which city's private council a dial targets. Per-face keys reduce cross-face inference; hiding paths from pin holders requires another/encrypted selector.
